Found during k130 (worker). Over Streamable HTTP, a connection error ("Request timeout", "Connection refused") reaches the agent without the "upstream NAME: " prefix every other rejection carries: Mojo's promisify rejects start_p's promise directly, so Http's $fail wrapper in _http_send_p is skipped for it. Done: every rejection of an Http request reads "upstream NAME: ...", a test in t/http.t for a refused connection and a timeout.

Done (mcp-hub-worker): in _http_send_p, $fail is the reject handler of the first then on start_p, so Mojo's own rejection reads 'upstream NAME: Connection refused' / 'upstream NAME: Request timeout'; nothing is prefixed twice, the stored error stays bare (503/status unchanged). SSE was already prefixed. Test t/http.t (http and sse refused, 1 s timeout), red 3/8. Not committed.

